# Safe player-facing tooltip/prose candidates.
enderutilities.tooltips.itemlocationboundmodular=- Sneak + right click to bind|lf- Alt + Shift + Toggle mode: Store the players's|lf  current position, including the yaw/pitch rotations|lf- Ctrl (+ Shift) + Toggle/scroll: Change selected Link Crystal|lf- Alt + Toggle: Toggle privacy mode on selected Link Crystal
item.enderutilities.builderswand.tooltips=- Can build with blocks from the player's or a linked external inventory|lf- Ctrl + scroll: Change mode|lf- Alt + scroll: Change the selected block type or the selected template/area|lf- Left click: set/unset primary position|lf- Two-corner modes: right click to set 2nd position or sneak + scroll while looking in a direction|lf- Sneak + clicking sets the position inside a block (this is only available in modes without block binding)|lf- Sneak + left click: Store the block type (where applicable)|lf- Shift + scroll: Change area dimensions in the looking direction (the primary position must be set for this!)|lf- Shift + Toggle (build modes): Toggle "move position after building"|lf- Alt + Toggle (some build modes): Toggle Replace on/off|lf- Shift + Toggle (area modes): Set area mirroring|lf- Shift + Toggle (Replace 3D): Toggle block type binding mode|lf- Ctrl + Alt + Toggle (Extend Continuous): Toggle "allow diagonals"|lf- Ctrl + Alt + Toggle (Paste): Toggle replace blocks|lf- Ctrl + Alt + Toggle (Delete): Toggle kill/remove entities|lf- Alt + Shift + Toggle: Toggle ghost block rendering|lf- Toggle: Flip the area around the looking axis|lf- Toggle (Copy mode): (Re-)name the current template|lf- Toggle (Paste/Delete modes): Set the area rotation to the current looking direction|lf- Toggle (Replace mode): Switch between Single/Area mode|lf- Ctrl + Alt + Shift + Scroll: Cycle selected Link Crystal|lf- Ctrl + Alt + Shift + Toggle (Copy): Toggle Chisels & Bits cross-world saving ON/OFF|lf  (leave it OFF unless you need to transfer builds into a separate world using the templates!)|lf- Alt + Shift + Scroll (Stack): Change the stack grid dimensions|lf- Alt + Shift + Scroll (Replace 3D): Change the replaced block type selection|lf- Sneak + right click on inventories to bind|lf- Ctrl + right click on air to place a helper block|lf- Saved templates are named by a unique ID generated for each wand
item.enderutilities.chairwand.tooltips=- Can spawn invisible "chair entities" that you can sit on|lf- Allows you to sit on your fancy custom C&B chairs for example|lf- Shift + scroll: Change spawned entity width|lf- Alt + scroll: Change spawned entity height|lf- Right click on a block to spawn a new chair entity|lf- Left click to kill the clicked-on chair entity
item.enderutilities.dolly.tooltips=- Can pick up and move blocks that have an inventory|lf- In Creative mode it can move any block
item.enderutilities.enderarrow.tooltips=- Hit mobs with the arrow for entertainment!|lf  (Chicken tennis maybe?)
item.enderutilities.enderbag.tooltips=- Sneak + right click to bind to a vanilla Ender Chest|lf- Ctrl (+ Shift) + Scroll: Change selected Link Crystal|lf- Doesn't currently work with other inventories|lf  because an event previously needed for the bag was removed in 1.10|lf  (new functionality is planned)
item.enderutilities.enderbow.tooltips=- Toggle mode key to switch between TP Target/TP Self|lf- Shift + Toggle: Toggle Bind Locking|lf  (prevents accidentally binding)|lf- Add a mob persistence module|lf  to prevent some mobs from despawning|lf- Repair in an Anvil with Enhanced Ender Alloy|lf- Needs Link Crystals to store locations|lf- Needs an Ender Capacitor for power
item.enderutilities.enderbucket.tooltips=- Toggle key: Cycle the operation mode|lf- Sneak + right click: Bind to tanks (in bind mode)|lf- Shift + Toggle: Switch between regular operation and tanks|lf- Tank mode chunk loads for 30 seconds on use|lf- In normal mode: right clicking a tank takes fluid from the|lf  tank, sneak + right clicking puts fluid to the tank|lf- Sneak + right click to bind|lf- Ctrl (+ Shift) + Toggle/scroll: Change selected Link Crystal
item.enderutilities.endercapacitor_0.tooltips=- Right click an Ender Crystal to charge (in The End)|lf- Or use an Ender Infuser|lf- Or build an Energy Bridge
item.enderutilities.endercapacitor_1.tooltips=- Right click an Ender Crystal to charge (in The End)|lf- Or use an Ender Infuser|lf- Or build an Energy Bridge
item.enderutilities.endercapacitor_2.tooltips=- Right click an Ender Crystal to charge (in The End)|lf- Or use an Ender Infuser|lf- Or build an Energy Bridge
item.enderutilities.enderlasso.tooltips=- Shift + Toggle: Toggle Bind Locking|lf  (prevents accidentally binding)|lf- Right click to teleport mobs|lf- Add a Jailer module to prevent mobs from despawning|lf- Needs Link Crystals to store locations|lf- Needs an Ender Capacitor for power
item.enderutilities.enderpart_creative_breaking.tooltips=- Can be installed to the Ender Pickaxe/Axe/Shovel|lf- Allows "creative-like" block breaking, meaning|lf  that blocks break instantly, but there is a small delay|lf  after each block, so that you don't accidentally|lf  destroy half your base when trying to break one block
item.enderutilities.enderpart_endercore_0_active.tooltips=- To obtain this item:|lf   Right click an Ender Crystal (in The End, the entity|lf   on top of the obsidian pillars) with an Inactive Ender Core
item.enderutilities.enderpart_endercore_1_active.tooltips=- To obtain this item:|lf   Right click an Ender Crystal (in The End, the entity|lf   on top of the obsidian pillars) with an Inactive Ender Core
item.enderutilities.enderpart_endercore_2_active.tooltips=- To obtain this item:|lf   Right click an Ender Crystal (in The End, the entity|lf   on top of the obsidian pillars) with an Inactive Ender Core
item.enderutilities.enderpart_endercore_0_inactive.tooltips=- Right click an Ender Crystal to activate (in The End)
item.enderutilities.enderpart_endercore_1_inactive.tooltips=- Right click an Ender Crystal to activate (in The End)
item.enderutilities.enderpart_endercore_2_inactive.tooltips=- Right click an Ender Crystal to activate (in The End)
item.enderutilities.enderpart_enderrelic.tooltips=- Spawns a new Ender Crystal|lf- Use on an Obsidian block on top of|lf  the obsidian pillars in The End|lf- In The End, it requires at least a 3x3x6 base of Obsidian|lf- Might be dangerous to your health...|lf- Can also spawn decorative Ender Crystals|lf  in other dimensions (no special requirements there)
item.enderutilities.enderpart_jailer.tooltips=- Rightclick a mob to prevent it from despawning|lf- Can be installed in some modular items|lf   to give them the same ability|lf- When installed in modular items, it doesn't get|lf   used up like it does when right clicking
item.enderutilities.enderpart_memorycard_items_0.tooltips=- Can store items in stacks up to 2^(bits) = 64|lf- Right click to toggle Public/Private|lf- Sneak + right click to clear owner data
item.enderutilities.enderpart_memorycard_items_1.tooltips=- Can store items in stacks up to 2^(bits) = 256|lf- Right click to toggle Public/Private|lf- Sneak + right click to clear owner data
item.enderutilities.enderpart_memorycard_items_2.tooltips=- Can store items in stacks up to 2^(bits) = 1024|lf- Right click to toggle Public/Private|lf- Sneak + right click to clear owner data
item.enderutilities.enderpart_memorycard_items_3.tooltips=- Can store items in stacks up to 2^(bits) = 4096|lf- Right click to toggle Public/Private|lf- Sneak + right click to clear owner data
item.enderutilities.enderpart_mobpersistence.tooltips=- Right click on a mob to prevent it from despawning|lf- Install into some modular items to achieve the same|lf- Using it directly consumes the item, modular items won't
item.enderutilities.enderpart_storage_key.tooltips=- Right click on (some) storage blocks to lock the slots
item.enderutilities.enderpart_storage_key_creative.tooltips=- Right click on (some) storage blocks to|lf  easily toggle the Creative mode on them
item.enderutilities.enderpearlreusable_elite.tooltips=Lets you fly! w00t!
item.enderutilities.enderporter.tooltips=- Shift + Toggle: Toggle Bind Locking|lf  (prevents accidentally binding)|lf- Can teleport the player or another|lf  entity inside the same dimension|lf- Self-TP: Hold right click until "charged", then release|lf- TP others: Sneak + left click the target|lf  (if the target is a player, they must sneak too)|lf- Needs Link Crystals to store locations|lf- Needs an Ender Capacitor for power
item.enderutilities.enderporter_advanced.tooltips=- Shift + Toggle: Toggle Bind Locking|lf  (prevents accidentally binding)|lf- Can teleport the player or another|lf  entity cross-dimensionally|lf- Self-TP: Hold right click until "charged", then release|lf- TP others: Sneak + left click the target|lf  (if the target is a player, they must sneak too)|lf- Needs Link Crystals to store locations|lf- Needs an Ender Capacitor for power
item.enderutilities.endertool_enderpickaxe.tooltips=- Add Efficiency V for instant mining of common|lf  blocks in the fast mode|lf- Fast mode uses two durability per mined block|lf- The tool will never break completely|lf- Repair in an anvil with one Advanced Ender Alloy and 15 levels|lf- Right click to place blocks from adjacent slot|lf- Toggle key: toggle between normal/fast mode|lf- Ctrl + Shift + Toggle: Toggle creative breaking mode on/off|lf- Shift + Toggle mode: cycle the drops handling mode|lf  - Normal: items drop normally|lf  - Player: items will be inserted directly to the player's|lf    inventory, if possible. If not, they will drop normally.|lf  - Remote: items will be teleported to|lf    the selected Link Crystal's destination, if possible.|lf- Player mode requires an active Basic Ender Core|lf- Remote mode requires either an active Enhanced|lf  Ender Core (inter-dimensional transport) or an active|lf  Advanced Ender Core (cross-dimensional transport)
item.enderutilities.endertool_enderaxe.tooltips=- Add Efficiency V for instant mining of common|lf  blocks in the fast mode|lf- Fast mode uses two durability per mined block|lf- The tool will never break completely|lf- Repair in an anvil with one Advanced Ender Alloy and 15 levels|lf- Right click to place blocks from adjacent slot|lf- Toggle key: toggle between normal/fast mode|lf- Ctrl + Shift + Toggle: Toggle creative breaking mode on/off|lf- Shift + Toggle mode: cycle the drops handling mode|lf  - Normal: items drop normally|lf  - Player: items will be inserted directly to the player's|lf    inventory, if possible. If not, they will drop normally.|lf  - Remote: items will be teleported to|lf    the selected Link Crystal's destination, if possible.|lf- Player mode requires an active Basic Ender Core|lf- Remote mode requires either an active Enhanced|lf  Ender Core (inter-dimensional transport) or an active|lf  Advanced Ender Core (cross-dimensional transport)
item.enderutilities.endertool_endershovel.tooltips=- Add Efficiency V for instant mining of common|lf  blocks in the fast mode|lf- Fast mode uses two durability per mined block|lf- The tool will never break completely|lf- Repair in an anvil with one Advanced Ender Alloy and 15 levels|lf- Right click to place blocks from adjacent slot|lf- Toggle key: toggle between normal/fast mode|lf- Ctrl + Shift + Toggle: Toggle creative breaking mode on/off|lf- Shift + Toggle mode: cycle the drops handling mode|lf  - Normal: items drop normally|lf  - Player: items will be inserted directly to the player's|lf    inventory, if possible. If not, they will drop normally.|lf  - Remote: items will be teleported to|lf    the selected Link Crystal's destination, if possible.|lf- Player mode requires an active Basic Ender Core|lf- Remote mode requires either an active Enhanced|lf  Ender Core (inter-dimensional transport) or an active|lf  Advanced Ender Core (cross-dimensional transport)
item.enderutilities.endertool_enderhoe.tooltips=- Can till and plant a 3x3 area in the "Fast" mode|lf- Can plant crops from player or linked inventory|lf  (to plant right click on the farmland|lf  and have something to plant in your|lf  inventory or the linked inventory)|lf- The tool will never break completely|lf- Repair in an anvil with one Advanced Ender Alloy and 15 levels|lf- Toggle mode key: toggle between 1x1 and 3x3 mode|lf- Shift + Toggle mode: cycle the inventory mode|lf  - Normal: No special functionality|lf  - Player: items will be inserted into/taken from the player's|lf    inventory, if possible. If not, they will drop normally.|lf  - Remote: items will be teleported to/from|lf    the selected Link Crystal's destination, if possible.|lf- Player mode requires an active Basic Ender Core|lf- Remote mode requires either an active Enhanced|lf  Ender Core (inter-dimensional transport) or an active|lf  Advanced Ender Core (cross-dimensional transport)
item.enderutilities.endersword.tooltips=- The sword will never break completely|lf- Repair in an anvil with one Advanced Ender Alloy and 15 levels|lf- Shift + Toggle mode: cycle the sword mode|lf  - Normal: no special functionality|lf  - Player: drops from killed mobs will be inserted|lf    directly to the player's inventory, if possible.|lf  - Remote: items will be teleported to|lf    the selected Link Crystal's destination, if possible.|lf  - Summon: Does minimal direct damage, spawns up to 3|lf    new Ender Fighters to attack the target.|lf- The Ender Fighters start to rage and attack players|lf  if there is no player holding an Ender Sword|lf  in the Summon mode within 32 blocks.|lf- Idle Ender Fighters disappear sometime after 10 seconds.|lf- Using a Name Tag on them makes them peaceful.|lf- Player mode requires an active Basic Ender Core|lf- Remote mode requires either an active Enhanced|lf  Ender Core (inter-dimensional transport) or an active|lf  Advanced Ender Core (cross-dimensional transport)
item.enderutilities.handybag.tooltips=- A bag that opens when you open the regular inventory|lf  and have an enabled Handy Bag in your inventory|lf- The first bag found (= hotbar first, then top-left-most first) will be used|lf- Sneak while opening the inventory to|lf  open the regular inventory instead (configurable to reverse)|lf- Toggle key: Toggle restock mode|lf- Shift + Toggle: Toggle pickup mode|lf- Alt + Shift + Toggle: Toggle locked state|lf  (a locked bag doesn't open when opening the inventory)|lf- Alt + Toggle mode: Toggle public/private|lf  (Note: this is stored per Memory Card!)|lf- Can be sneak + right clicked on inventories to dump or take items|lf   To dump, the restock mode should be active and pickup disabled|lf   To suck in items, the pickup mode should be active and restock disabled|lf- Uses item type Memory Cards|lf- Max stack size depends on the used Memory Card tier|lf- Regular bag has 27 slots, Large has 55|lf- Tip: Middle click to swap two slots|lf- The "Block Quick Actions" button disables the quick move buttons|lf   and also the pickup/restock features in that bag section|lf- Update Items calls the update method on all the items in the bag (section)|lf   This may be useful for some "effect items" so they work while in the bag.|lf   However it's recommended to keep it disabled normally, as it increases server load somewhat|lf- The restock mode should also be disabled when not needed, to save server performance
item.enderutilities.icemelter_basic.tooltips=- Melts Ice into a still water source block|lf- Make Ice great again!
item.enderutilities.icemelter_super.tooltips=- Melts Ice into a still water source block,|lf  without even causing a block update!|lf- Water curtains Ahoy!
item.enderutilities.inventoryswapper.tooltips=- Can swap the player's inventory contents with|lf  the currently selected Memory Card's contents|lf- Can also swap with block inventories on sneak + right click|lf- Uses ONLY 6 B item-type Memory Cards!|lf- Right click to open GUI|lf- The hotkeys work even when the item is not selected or in the hotbar|lf- Toggle key alone: Execute a swap operation|lf- Ctrl (+ Shift) + Toggle/scroll: Change selected Memory Card|lf   or execute a Cycle operation when in Cycle mode|lf- Alt + toggle: Change card/cycle backwards|lf  (same as Ctrl + Shift + toggle, but a bit easier on the fingers)|lf- Shift + Toggle/scroll: Cycle slot selection preset|lf- Ctrl + Alt + Shift + Toggle: Toggle the Cycle mode on/off|lf- Alt + Shift + Toggle: Toggle locked/unlocked
item.enderutilities.linkcrystal_0.tooltips=- Sneak + right click to bind to a location|lf- Alt + Shift + Toggle mode: Store the players's|lf  current position, INCLUDING the yaw/pitch rotations|lf- Alt + Toggle mode to toggle public/private|lf- Tip: Rename in an anvil; the name is usually|lf  shown after the container item's name
item.enderutilities.linkcrystal_1.tooltips=- Sneak + right click to bind to a block|lf- Alt + Toggle mode to toggle public/private|lf- Tip: Rename in an anvil; the name is usually|lf  shown after the container item's name
item.enderutilities.linkcrystal_2.tooltips=- Allows pairing the Portals into pairs,|lf   instead of the normal arbitrary destination location|lf- Sneak + right click on a EnU Portal block to bind|lf  (Portal block means the blocks that are created when a Portal is activated)
item.enderutilities.livingmanipulator.tooltips=- Can store and release mobs|lf- Ctrl + (Shift +) Toggle/scroll: Cycle selected Memory Card|lf- Shift + Toggle/scroll: Cycle selected mob|lf- Toggle key: Change mode (Normal/Capture only/Release only)|lf- If a Jailer module is installed, then the released mobs|lf   don't despawn like they might normally (for example hostiles)
item.enderutilities.mobharness.tooltips=- Right click a mob to ride it|lf- Sneak + right click to 'store' a mob,|lf  then sneak + right click another mob to mount|lf  the first one on top of the second one|lf- Sneak + right click twice on the same mob|lf  to mount it on top of yourself|lf- Sneak + right click a mob that is riding|lf  something to dismount it|lf- Look down and sneak + right click|lf  to clear a 'binding'|lf- Look up and sneak + right click|lf  to dismount the mob riding you
item.enderutilities.nullifier.tooltips=- 9 slots, max 1024 items per slot|lf- Automatically picks up matching items|lf- Items that exist in the Nullifier but can't fit|lf  into the existing slots, will be deleted|lf- Toggle key: open the GUI|lf- Shift + Toggle: Toggle disabled status|lf- Ctrl + Toggle or Scroll: Change selected slot
item.enderutilities.pet_contract_blank.tooltips=- Allows transferring the ownership of tameable mobs|lf- The owner must right click the mob to "sign the contract"|lf- Another player can then claim ownership of that mob|lf   by right clicking it with the signed contract
item.enderutilities.pickupmanager.tooltips=- Controls which items can be picked up|lf- Can transport picked up items to a remote inventory|lf  and also allows manually sending items from the "send slot"|lf- Toggle key: Toggle locked/unlocked state|lf- Shift + Toggle/scroll: Cycle filter preset|lf- Ctrl (+ Shift) + Toggle/scroll: Change selected Link Crystal|lf- Alt + Toggle: Toggle privacy mode on selected Link Crystal|lf- Sneak + right click: bind to an inventory|lf- Needs Link Crystals to store target locations|lf- NOTE: Needs an Ender Capacitor for power when sending items remotely!
item.enderutilities.portalscaler.tooltips=- Will change the Nether Portal teleportation scale factor,|lf  if you right click with it while standing in a portal.|lf- To change the scaling factor:|lf  - First select the item in your hotbar|lf  - Look at the direction of the axis you want to change (x/y/z)|lf  - Then press and hold Alt + Shift and use the mouse wheel|lf  - Or press Alt + Shift (+ Ctrl) + Toggle mode|lf- Can also light up and shut down portals|lf  (right click a portal block/the obsidian frame|lf  while NOT standing in the portal)
item.enderutilities.quickstacker.tooltips=- Quick stacks items from the player's|lf  inventory to nearby inventories|lf- Max range is 4 blocks horizontally, 3 vertically|lf- Press the Toggle Mode button to activate|lf- Works also while not in hand|lf- Normally moves only matching items|lf- Sneak while activating to move non-matching items too|lf- Can also be sneak + right clicked on|lf  inventories to quick stack to that inventory
item.enderutilities.ruler.tooltips=Measure distances and visualize positions|lf- Left/right click to set start/end position|lf- Sneak to target the block, not the empty space|lf- Shift + scroll: Cycle selected point|lf- Ctrl + scroll: Cycle selected Memory Card|lf- Alt + Toggle: Toggle render when unselected|lf- Ctrl + Alt + Toggle: Toggle distance mode|lf- Alt + Shift + Toggle: Toggle render all points|lf- Just Toggle: Toggle "render with all" for selected point
item.enderutilities.syringe_paralyzer.tooltips=- Paralyzes mobs (sets the NoAI flag)
item.enderutilities.syringe_passifier.tooltips=- Passifies mobs, by removing their target AI tasks|lf- If anything attacks a passified mob, it will|lf   "become angry" and return to its normal hostile state
item.enderutilities.syringe_stimulant.tooltips=- Un-paralyzes mobs (removes the NoAI flag)
item.enderutilities.void_pickaxe.tooltips=- Destroyed blocks drop nothing, not even inventory contents|lf- Also works in Creative mode|lf- Add an Efficiency V enchant for|lf  insta-mining of most blocks in the Fast mode|lf- Toggle key: Change between Normal and Fast mode
tile.enderutilities.asu.tooltips=- Adjustable number of slots, 1 to 27|lf- Adjustable max stack size, up to 1024
tile.enderutilities.barrel.tooltips=- Sneak + right click to open the GUI|lf- Middle click (pick block) with an empty main hand|lf   and a block in the offhand to apply camouflage|lf- Sneak while doing that to remove the camouflage
tile.enderutilities.creation_station.tooltips=- Combines two crafting tables, two furnaces and some modular storage|lf- Has recipe memory, quick fill crafting grids etc. functionality
tile.enderutilities.draw_bridge.tooltips=- Extends or contracts a line of blocks|lf- Max length is 64 for normal, 32 for Advanced|lf- Advanced version can use different blocks for each position|lf- Can be camouflaged by right clicking with an empty main hand,|lf  while holding the camo block in the off hand|lf- Sneak + right click with an empty hand to remove the camo block
tile.enderutilities.ender_furnace.tooltips=- A lot faster than a vanilla furnace|lf  (3 seconds per item in normal mode, 1 second in fast)|lf- Can use Ender Pearls, Eyes of Ender and Blaze Powder|lf  as fuel in addition to the normal furnace fuels|lf- Can also use lava as fuel from fluid containers|lf  such as the Ender Bucket or portable tanks|lf- Can operate without fuel (1 item per 60 seconds)|lf- Slow mode cooks 1.5x the items per fuel|lf  compared to a vanilla furnace|lf- Fast mode uses fuel 6x faster than slow mode over time|lf  (= 0.75x the items per fuel vs. vanilla)|lf- Can output directly to the owner's vanilla Ender Chest
tile.enderutilities.ender_infuser.tooltips=- Can charge the Ender Capacitors|lf- Use Ender Pearls or Eyes of Ender as "fuel"|lf- One of the three charging options atm
tile.enderutilities.ender_elevator.tooltips=- Teleports an entity to the closest matching colored elevator|lf- Maximum range is 256 vertically, 64 horizontally|lf- Jump to go up, sneak to go down|lf- Can also be activated by redstone (rising edge)|lf- Power level of < 8 goes up and >= 8 goes down|lf- Can be re-colored by right clicking with a dye|lf- Can be camouflaged by right clicking with an empty main hand,|lf  while holding the camo block in the off hand|lf- Sneak + right click with an empty hand to remove the camo block
tile.enderutilities.energy_bridge_transmitter.tooltips=- An active Energy Bridge gives automatic|lf  Ender Capacitor recharging, when the capacitor is|lf  installed in a modular item|lf  and the item is in the player's inventory|lf- You need one Transmitter in The End|lf- It doesn't need to be chunk loaded|lf  (it doesn't actually actively do anything)|lf- Build the Transmitter around an Ender Crystal|lf  (on top of the Obsidian pillars in The End)|lf- Leave two blocks of air above the Crystal|lf  and then place the Transmitter|lf- Place four Resonators on the same level as|lf  the Ender Crystal, two blocks of air between them|lf- The Resonators must face the Crystal|lf  (place them when looking out)|lf- There can only be transparent blocks above|lf  the Transmitter all the way up to the sky|lf- There must not be any blocks|lf  between the Resonators and/or the center
tile.enderutilities.energy_bridge_receiver.tooltips=- An active Energy Bridge gives automatic|lf  Ender Capacitor recharging, when the capacitor is|lf  installed in a modular item|lf  and the item is in the player's inventory|lf- You need one Receiver in each dimension you|lf  want the recharging to work in|lf- It doesn't need to be chunk loaded|lf  (it doesn't actually actively do anything)|lf- Place the Receiver in the middle|lf- Place four Resonators on the same level as|lf  the Receiver, two blocks of air between them|lf- The Resonators must face the Receiver|lf  (place them when looking out)|lf- There can only be transparent blocks above|lf  and below the Receiver all the way down|lf  to Bedrock and up to the sky|lf- There must not be any blocks|lf  between the Resonators and/or the Receiver
tile.enderutilities.energy_bridge_resonator.tooltips=- See the description for the Transmitter and Receiver|lf- There must only be air "between" the Resonators|lf  (ie. where the beams will form, diagonally between Resonators|lf  and between the Resonators and the Receiver)
tile.enderutilities.inserter_filtered.tooltips=- Sort of like a pipe, but not really a pipe|lf- Will try to insert items to enabled sides first|lf- Will then fall back to inserting items to its front side|lf- If multiple sides are enabled, will cycle them in order|lf  (= evenly distributes the items)|lf- Sneak + right click with an empty hand to toggle the side outputs|lf- Has filters for controlling what is allowed on the side outputs|lf- Items not allowed through the filters go to the front side|lf- The filters are (at least for now) common for all sides
tile.enderutilities.inserter_normal.tooltips=- Sort of like a pipe, but not really a pipe|lf- Will try to insert items to enabled sides first|lf- Will then fall back to inserting items to its front side|lf- If multiple sides are enabled, will cycle them in order|lf  (= evenly distributes the items)|lf- Sneak + right click with an empty hand to toggle the side outputs
tile.enderutilities.floor_cracked.tooltips=- Bad quality floor...|lf- Items and XP orbs will slip through the cracks
tile.enderutilities.frame.tooltips=- The portal can be any shape or size|lf  (within reason, there are configurable limits)|lf- It just needs to form a closed loop for the frame|lf- Can be camouflaged by right clicking with an empty main hand,|lf  while holding the camo block in the off hand|lf- Sneak + right click with an empty hand to remove the camo block
tile.enderutilities.handy_chest.tooltips=- Easier inventory management and lots|lf  of storage space|lf- Middle click to swap two large stacks|lf- Shift + click a move button|lf  to set it as the quick action|lf- Double-left-click the chest to|lf  execute the selected quick action|lf- The owner of a Memory Card can|lf  right click the card selection button to lock|lf  that card into the slot, so nobody else can|lf  take the card itself out of that slot|lf- A chest with locked-in-place cards is unbreakable
tile.enderutilities.jsu.tooltips=- Can only store normally non-stackable items|lf- 270 slots of storage space, max 256 items per stack
tile.enderutilities.msu_0.tooltips=- 1 slot, which can store large amounts of items|lf- Middle click the slots in creative mode to fill/clear the slot|lf  - 1 item in cursor => grow the stack size by x10|lf  - More than 1 item in cursor => fill/clear the slot
tile.enderutilities.msu_1.tooltips=- 9 slots, which can store large amounts of items|lf- Middle click the slots in creative mode to fill/clear the slot|lf  - 1 item in cursor => grow the stack size by x10|lf  - More than 1 item in cursor => fill/clear the slot
tile.enderutilities.memory_chest.tooltips=Each slot can be locked to an item type
tile.enderutilities.portal_panel.tooltips=- Used to activate a Portal made of Portal Frame blocks|lf- The panel must be placed on a Portal Frame block|lf- That frame must connect to the actual portal frame loop/rim|lf  via a _continuous_ "path" of Portal Frame blocks|lf  (no diagonal gaps allowed in it)|lf- However the portal frame rim itself can have "diagonal corners"|lf- Uses either Location or Portal type Link Crystals for the destination
tile.enderutilities.molecular_exciter.tooltips=- Turns blocks infront of itself into falling|lf  blocks on redstone pulse or block update|lf- Needs a redstone signal to be active
tile.enderutilities.phasing.tooltips=- Changes state between solid and non-solid based on redstone signal
tile.enderutilities.phasing_inverted.tooltips=- Changes state between solid and non-solid based on redstone signal
tile.enderutilities.quick_stacker_advanced.tooltips=- A more configurable, stationary version of Quick Stacker
tile.enderutilities.sound_block.tooltips=- Yes, it plays sounds...|lf- Select any sound from the registered sounds|lf- Adjustable pitch and volume
tile.enderutilities.tool_workstation.tooltips=- Used to access/change the modules in modular items|lf- Can also rename any item for free
enderutilities.tooltip.placementproperties.tooltips= |lf§f*** Placement Properties ***§r|lf- (Shift +) Toggle key to change property selection|lf- Shift/Ctrl/Alt + scroll to change the value
enderutilities.tooltip.item.andmorestacksnotlisted=  ... and %s%d%s more stacks not listed
enderutilities.tooltip.item.build.circle=Circle (INCOMPLETE - doesn't do anything atm)
enderutilities.tooltip.item.memorycard.items.stackcount=Storing %d stacks / %s items in total
enderutilities.tooltip.item.usetoolworkstation=Use the Tool Workstation to add or remove modules
enderutilities.chat.message.areasavedtotemplate=Area saved to template %d
